## Featured AWS Cloud Projects

### 01 | Hosting a Static Website on Amazon S3

**Technologies:** Amazon S3, Static Website Hosting, Bucket Policies, AWS Cloud Architecture

**Business challenge:** A city relied on on-premises servers to host a public beach wave-conditions website. Frequent server failures affected availability, while provisioning new infrastructure took months.

**Solution:** Configured Amazon S3 static website hosting to support a managed hosting approach without maintaining dedicated web servers.

**Implementation highlights:**
- Reviewed website objects in an S3 bucket.
- Configured static website hosting with index and error documents.
- Examined public-read permissions and S3 Block Public Access settings.
- Completed an independent S3 object-renaming challenge.
- Successfully passed the AWS SimuLearn DIY validation.
- Documented security considerations, operational limitations, and potential improvements.

**Validation:** DIY challenge passed. End-to-end browser testing has not yet been recorded.

**Project type:** AWS SimuLearn guided implementation with validated DIY challenge.

